# Force a single, consistent line ending in the repository regardless of which OS commits —
# this session runs Linux (LF), Maxime builds on Windows (checkouts default to CRLF without this
# file). Without it, `git status` on Windows shows the entire tree as "modified" after any merge
# from a Linux-authored bundle (verified 18/08/2026: 74 files, equal insertions/deletions, same
# content — pure line-ending noise, not real changes). `text=auto` lets Git normalize text files
# to LF in the repository itself and convert on checkout per the platform's usual convention;
# binary-ish/generated files are excluded so they are never touched.
* text=auto

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.bundle binary
